From 42299c5e9e44b8cef69f152a1989199119d79c90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:25:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] A primary mouse or pen press on a rail session row that is
 not the one shown opens that session's store, so the outline, row and first
 two screens of rows are already on the wire while the release is still to
 come and the click's mount of the session screen and composer runs beside the
 read instead of ahead of it, since the read's first fetch otherwise waits
 behind every microtask of that mount; a touch press opens nothing because it
 often starts a scroll, activation stays on click, and the app's line budget
 is the measured 107,777.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QtZVtcNTgBwKhSN8i2v1w2
